.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_OP_BUILDER_NEW 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_new ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_input ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_input_connection ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_output ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_output_connection ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_input_sparse ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_output_sparse ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_set_notify ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_build ,
.Nm dtfl_op_builder_index
.Nd build a generic timely dataflow operator
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft dtfl_op_builder *
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_new "dtfl_scope *s" "const char *name"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input "dtfl_op_builder *b" "dtfl_stream *in" "dtfl_pact pact"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input_connection "dtfl_op_builder *b" "dtfl_stream *in" "dtfl_pact pact" "const uint64_t *const *summaries"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output "dtfl_op_builder *b" "const dtfl_type *type"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output_connection "dtfl_op_builder *b" "const dtfl_type *type" "const uint64_t *const *summaries"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input_sparse "dtfl_op_builder *b" "dtfl_stream *in" "dtfl_pact pact" "size_t n" "const size_t *outputs" "const uint64_t *const *summaries"
.Ft dtfl_stream *
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output_sparse "dtfl_op_builder *b" "const dtfl_type *type" "size_t n" "const size_t *inputs" "const uint64_t *const *summaries"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_set_notify "dtfl_op_builder *b" "size_t input" "dtfl_interest interest"
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_build "dtfl_op_builder *b" "dtfl_logic_fn logic" "void *ctx" "void (*ctx_free)(void *)"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_index "const dtfl_op_builder *b"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions build an operator of arbitrary shape inside a scope's
.Fn dtfl_build_fn
callback.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_new
reserves an operator slot in
.Fa s
with the given
.Fa name
and returns a builder.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input
adds an input reading from
.Fa in
through the parallelization contract
.Fa pact
.Pq Xr dtfl_pact_pipeline 3 ,
and returns the input's index.
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input_connection
is the same but takes, for each existing output, a path summary of
.Fn dtfl_summary_depth
words or
.Dv NULL
for no connection; a plain
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input
promises the identity summary to every output.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output
adds an output carrying records of
.Fa type ,
which is retained, and returns the resulting stream.
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output_connection
takes a summary per existing input the same way.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input_sparse
and
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output_sparse
take the connection as
.Fa n
pairs instead: entry
.Fa k
connects the new port to existing output
.Fa outputs Ns [ Fa k ]
(or existing input
.Fa inputs Ns [ Fa k ] )
with summary
.Fa summaries Ns [ Fa k ] .
Ports not named are not connected, and a port named twice keeps the
antichain of its summaries.
Their cost is linear in
.Fa n
rather than in the number of existing ports, which matters for
operators with many ports.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_set_notify
sets the frontier interest of an input: whether the operator is
scheduled on a frontier change always, only while it holds a
capability, or never.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_build
installs the operator and consumes the builder.
.Fa logic
runs on every schedule with an operator handle valid only during the
call
.Pq Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3
and
.Fa ctx ;
returning
.Dv true
reports the operator incomplete, so the runtime keeps it live even with
empty input frontiers and no held capabilities.
.Fa ctx_free ,
if not
.Dv NULL ,
runs when the operator is dropped.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_index
returns the operator's scope-local index.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_new
returns a builder the
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_build
call consumes.
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input
and
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input_connection
and
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_input_sparse
return the new input's index.
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output ,
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output_connection
and
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_output_sparse
return the output stream, owned by the scope.
.Fn dtfl_op_builder_index
returns the operator's index.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A map operator that adds one to each input record:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static bool logic(dtfl_op *op, void *ctx) {
	dtfl_message *m;
	dtfl_cap_drop(dtfl_op_initial_cap(op, 0));
	while ((m = dtfl_op_input_next(op, 0)) != NULL) {
		dtfl_cap *c = dtfl_op_input_cap(op, 0, 0);
		dtfl_session *s = dtfl_op_session(op, 0, c);
		dtfl_session_give_message(s, m);
		dtfl_session_close(s);
		dtfl_cap_drop(c);
	}
	return false;
}

dtfl_op_builder *b = dtfl_op_builder_new(scope, "Map");
dtfl_op_builder_input(b, in, dtfl_pact_pipeline());
dtfl_stream *out = dtfl_op_builder_output(b, dtfl_type_u64());
dtfl_op_builder_build(b, logic, NULL, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These functions do not return error codes; a misuse, such as a summary
that names an output that does not exist, is a contract violation that
reaches the panic hook
.Pq Xr dtfl_set_panic_hook 3 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_cap_delayed 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_pact_pipeline 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_stream_scope 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_worker_dataflow 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C form of timely's
.Vt OperatorBuilder
.Pq builder_rc.rs ,
layered on the raw
.Vt OperatorBuilder
of builder_raw.rs.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A builder and the operator it installs belong to the worker thread that
runs the build callback and must not be shared.
